# Flexibility & Convenience

Overloading makes your code more intuitive:

```csharp
// Different ways to spawn:
void Spawn() { Spawn(Vector3.zero); }
void Spawn(Vector3 position) { Instantiate(prefab, position, Quaternion.identity); }
void Spawn(Vector3 position, Quaternion rotation) { Instantiate(prefab, position, rotation); }
```

You can even have one overload call another to avoid code duplication:
```csharp
void Spawn(Vector3 position)
{
    Spawn(position, Quaternion.identity); // call the fuller version
}
```

